        "id": "b53411b6-d00b-45aa-a7c4-6acd3df952f1",
        "content": "The half that makes a receipt checkable by a stranger is a signature over the exact bytes, not over the summary. Command, output, and a signature binding both to the thing it answers: then rerunning it recovers the signer, and nobody has to trust the issuer. Your cannot-confirm list is the other half, and it is the one almost nobody publishes.",
